DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The "compatible" property of the device tree node is used to identify the
     type of the device the node represents.  The property is a list of one or
     more strings that represent hardware types the device is compatible with.
     The common format for such strings is "vendor,hardware" where "vendor" is
     an abbreviated name of the manufacturer and "hardware" is a device iden‐
     tifier, for instance, "fsl" for "Freescale" and "imx6ul-i2c" for the I2C
     controller.  More than one string is required for compatibility with
     older revisions of the driver.  If hardware revision B is backward com‐
     patible with revision A device tree node can signal this compatibility by
     providing both "vndr,hrdwrA" and "vndr,hrdwrB" strings in the "compati‐
     bile" property value.  This way older driver can use features available
     only in revision A, and the new version of the driver can take advantage
     of revision B feature set.

     ooffww__bbuuss__iiss__ccoommppaattiibbllee() returns 1 if the _c_o_m_p_a_t_s_t_r value occurs in the
     "compatible" property list of the device tree node associated with the
     device _d_e_v, and 0 otherwise.

     ooffww__bbuuss__iiss__ccoommppaattiibbllee__ssttrriicctt() return 1 if the "compatible" property of
     the device tree node associated with the device _d_e_v consists of only one
     string and this string is equal to _c_o_m_p_a_t_s_t_r, and 0 otherwise.

     ooffww__bbuuss__nnooddee__iiss__ccoommppaattiibbllee() returns 1 if the _c_o_m_p_a_t_s_t_r value occurs in
     the "compatible" property list of the device tree node _n_o_d_e, and 0 other‐
     wise.

     ooffww__bbuuss__sseeaarrcchh__ccoommppaattiibbllee() returns pointer to the first entry of the
     _c_o_m_p_a_t table whose ocd_str field occurs in "compatible" property of the
     device tree node associated with the device _d_e_v.  The _c_o_m_p_a_t table is an
     array of struct ofw_compat_data elements defined as follows:

           struct ofw_compat_data {
                   const char *ocd_str;
                   uintptr_t  ocd_data;
           };
     The _c_o_m_p_a_t table must be terminated by the entry with ocd_str set to
     NULL.  If the device tree node is not compatible with any of the entries,
     the function returns the pointer to the terminating entry.

